{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3363","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3363","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3363\",\"parent_revision\":\"c27d1822f5e239901d0f14285571cabb06ed5777b67ceccb8b8a8452392c2d8a\",\"root_revision\":\"c27d1822f5e239901d0f14285571cabb06ed5777b67ceccb8b8a8452392c2d8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-01\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nConfirmed via `pytest -W error::ResourceWarning`: `TestBacklogBackendCapabilityContract` in `tests_backlog/test_backlog_backend_capability_contract.py` (pre-existing, unrelated to PR #3360's changes) leaks a `sqlite3.Connection` on every `create_backend(\\\"sqlite\\\")` call \u2014 `SQLiteBackend()`'s connection has no lifecycle owner in that class's test bodies, so it triggers `ResourceWarning`/`PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning` at GC time, which fails this repo's strict warning-as-error validation policy (AGENTS.md #18).\\n\\nThis is the same pattern PR #3360 just fixed locally in two other files (`tests/test_github_extras_capability_gate.py` via a fixture, `tests_backlog/test_backlog_backend_capability_contract.py`'s new `TestGitHubExtrasCapabilityContract` class via a `_close_if_sqlite()` helper called in `finally`), but `create_backend(\\\"sqlite\\\")` is called from many more test files across `tests/` and `tests_backlog/` \u2014 grep for `create_backend(` to find the full list. `SQLiteBackend` has no public `close()` method; every caller directly closes the private `_conn` attribute (see `tests_backlog/test_local_content_backends.py`'s `local_provider` fixture for the established pattern).\\n\\nRoot-cause fix options, not decided: (1) add a public `SQLiteBackend.close()` and audit every `create_backend(\\\"sqlite\\\")` call site to use it, or (2) build a shared pytest fixture wrapping `create_backend()` with parametrized cleanup and migrate call sites onto it. Flagged for triage \u2014 multi-file, not a single trivial edit.\\n\\nDoes not currently block the default `pytest` run (no `filterwarnings = error` in `pyproject.toml`'s pytest config) \u2014 only surfaces under an explicit `-W error::ResourceWarning` run, which AGENTS.md #18 implies some validation step performs.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Pre-existing issue discovered during PR #3360 (backlog #2287 slice 1) \u2014 per plugins/holistic-linting's pre-existing-issues-protocol.md, non-blocking findings get recorded, not silently dropped.\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8d4e8ac380a0e47622a34e9f838d9230dc923db6109a4ae4a6a435f39b832b31\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABR0jSzQ\"}"}